      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community once had its own high school with black‑and‑white leopards as colors and mascot before merging into Perry Central in 1962.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopold%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Leopold sits fifteen miles north of the Ohio River and rises 720 feet above sea level, offering a mild climate similar to their homeland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
